# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the DamiaProdan website.

## Changes Made

### Created Files:
- **package.json** - Added project configuration with @vercel/analytics dependency
- **.gitignore** - Created to exclude node_modules and build artifacts from version control

### Modified Files:
- **index.html** - Added Vercel Web Analytics scripts in the `<head>` section just before the closing tag

### Dependencies Installed:
- **@vercel/analytics** (v1.3.1) - Official Vercel Web Analytics package

## Implementation Details

Since this is a vanilla HTML/JavaScript project (not using a framework like Next.js or React), I followed the official Vercel documentation's instructions for HTML/Vanilla JavaScript projects:

1. **Fetched Latest Documentation**: Retrieved the current installation guide from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
2. **Created package.json**: Set up a basic package.json to manage the @vercel/analytics dependency
3. **Added Analytics Script**: Inserted the following code in the HTML `<head>` section:
   ```html
   <!-- Vercel Web Analytics -->
   <script>
     window.va = window.va || function () { (window.vaq = window.vaq || []).push(arguments); };
   </script>
   <script defer src="/_vercel/insights/script.js"></script>
   ```

## Testing

- ✅ Ran `npm install` successfully - @vercel/analytics installed without issues
- ✅ Ran `npm test` - All tests passed (no test suite configured, returns exit 0)
- ✅ Verified HTML structure remains intact
- ✅ Generated package-lock.json for dependency locking

## Next Steps

After deploying to Vercel:
1. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard under the Analytics section
2. Verify tracking is working by checking Network tab for requests to `/_vercel/insights/view`
3. View analytics data in the Vercel dashboard

## Notes

- The implementation preserves all existing code structure
- The analytics script is loaded asynchronously (using `defer`) to avoid blocking page rendering
- The script will automatically track page views once deployed to Vercel
- Lock file (package-lock.json) has been updated and should be committed for consistent dependency resolution
